  "summary": "I’m a digital developer and strategist working at the intersection of technology, data, and business planning.\n \nSince 2013, I’ve been with the Air Line Pilots Association, Int'l, where my role has grown from website coordination into a broader digital and strategic function. Today, I lead and support initiatives across digital development, data and business intelligence, and organizational strategy, helping turn complex information into practical tools and better decisions.\n \nMy work includes building and managing web platforms, developing custom solutions, and shaping digital and content strategies. I’ve also taken on a key role in data governance and analytics, bringing more structure and consistency to how data is collected and used.\n \nAt my core, I’m a problem solver. I focus on identifying gaps, then building the systems, processes, or tools needed to close them.\n \nI started my career in web and print design, which still shapes how I think about user experience and communication today. I hold a BS in Journalism and Electronic Media from the University of Tennessee.",
