      "description": "ALPA is the world’s largest airline pilot union representing 64k+ pilots at ~40 North American airlines. In this role, I am responsible for managing a portfolio of private microsites built using Sitecore, DotNetNuke, Evoq, WordPress, HTML/CSS, and jQuery. The sites are used for communications from the union to its members, with some sites consisting of 100s of pages.\n\nIn addition to the microsites, I also oversee digital communication across email (RealMagnet, Lyris, Evoq), SMS, push, and social media (Hootsuite). I have also been a driver of our analytics capabilities and provide ad hoc analysis to improve our engagement and to inform strategy.\n\nProject Highlights:\n• Successfully advocated for introduction of analytics capabilities for both web and email. Introduced Google Analytics and built out analytics dashboards and reporting for weekly/monthly/quarterly/annual reports. Analytics-driven content decision making resulted in 20% increase in pageviews since 2019 (250k+ views). \n\n• Contributed to a demo for a 40” touchscreen kiosk scheduled for placement within 10+ FedEx crewrooms, featuring news tickers, QR codes, and various communications from the union. \n\n• Introduced responsive email templates, increased engaging content, and optimized email send times based on analysis of email open data that led to email open rate growth from~50% in 2014 to ~75% in 2022. \n\n• Built the public site for a paid social campaign to support pilot negotiations and drive traffic to a niche microsite that resulted in 500k-1m social impressions and several thousand unique visitors per week.",
